course: dictionary
lesson: 11763
title: Barehanded: only your hands
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Barehanded is made from two words: bare, meaning with nothing covering it, and hand. So barehanded means using only your hands, with no gloves, tools or weapons. «Sam caught the slippery frog barehanded in the pond.» Sam did not use a net or a bucket. He used only his hands.
explain: Look at the clues in the sentence. «The knight fought the dragon barehanded.» A knight usually has a sword and armour, so the word barehanded tells you he had none of them. Read the words around barehanded to find the clue, then swap in your meaning to check it still makes sense.
explain: Barehanded can describe a thing or an action. «A barehanded catch» is an adjective. «She caught it barehanded» is an adverb. It is also sometimes written as bare-handed, with a hyphen.
fact: Barehanded means using only your hands, without gloves, tools or weapons.
fact: «Barehanded» can be an adjective («a barehanded catch») or an adverb («he caught it barehanded»).
fact: It is also written as «bare-handed», with a hyphen.
fact: Safety: «Never pick up broken glass barehanded.» Gloves protect your skin from cuts.
fact: The phrase «catch barehanded» means to catch something using only your hands.
exercise: «Sam caught the frog barehanded in the pond.» What does barehanded mean here? | *Using only his hands, with no net or gloves | Using a net with a long handle | Standing very still in the water | Wearing thick gloves
exercise: Ali says, «Never pick up broken glass barehanded.» Why? | It is quicker to use your feet | *Your skin can get cut | Glass is too light to hold | Gloves make glass break
exercise: Ella says barehanded means in a hurry. What is the right meaning? | *Using only your hands, without gloves, tools or weapons | Carefully and with a tool | Wearing a hat | Very fast
test: «The fisherman caught the eel barehanded.» Find and copy the one word that tells us he used no tools. | fisherman | eel | caught | *barehanded
test: What does «catch barehanded» mean? | *To catch with only your hands | To catch while wearing boxing gloves | To catch with a big net | To catch it and throw it back
exam: Which sentence means he used no gloves or tools? | He picked the berries with a pair of tongs. | He picked the berries with a big basket. | *He picked the berries barehanded. | He picked the berries while wearing thick gloves.
